{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLqtYrZiqm3Rz4cdwJHw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: `limit(2**(1/x), x, 0, dir='-')` now returns `0`.\n\n**Cause:** in `sympy/series/limits.py`, the helper `Limit.pow_heuristics` worked out its sub-limits without passing the direction along, so it always took the right-hand limit. For `2**(1/x)` it computed `exp(limit(log(2)/x, x, 0))`, which is the `+` side and gives `oo`.\n\n**Fix:** `pow_heuristics` now takes a `dir` argument and passes it to all of its internal `limit` calls. The one place that calls it passes the direction through. The change is six lines in that one file.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `limit(2**(1/x), x, 0, '-')` gives `0`\n- `limit(2**(1/x), x, 0, '+')` gives `oo`\n- `limit(2**x, x, oo)` gives `oo`\n- `limit((1+x)**(1/x), x, 0, '-')` gives `E`\n- `sympy/series/tests/test_limits.py` and `test_gruntz.py`: 211 passed, 3 skipped, 6 xfailed, 2 deselected, no failures.\n\nThe second example in the issue, `limit(2**x, x, -oo)`, already returned `0` in this checkout before my change, so whatever broke it in 1.13.3 seems to have been fixed already. It still returns `0`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":271,"cache_read_input_tokens":25302,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":271},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cbca4a07-7d00-4778-b80c-89fd090c7ed2","uuid":"a94923e9-c64f-4ffe-9de4-5410355b3976","timestamp":"2026-11-24T00:56:50.719Z","request_id":"req_011ChLqtYbvpexbvh1ZciZ4B"}
